                            <comment id="14386077" author="rakeshr" created="Mon, 30 Mar 2015 01:46:00 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=hustlmsp&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;hustlmsp&quot;&gt;hustlmsp&lt;/a&gt; since this is a straight fix and not harming any other flows, I agree with your point. Please go ahead to fix this case.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thanks &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=zhaijia&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;zhaijia&quot;&gt;zhaijia&lt;/a&gt; for catching this.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Just one comment. Should we complete the call back by calling &lt;tt&gt;ensembleUpdatedCb#processResult(Code.UnexpectedConditionException, null, null);&lt;/tt&gt; if the condition falls in else block ?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;+        &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;else&lt;/span&gt; {
+            LOG.warn(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;Bookie {} doesn&apos;t exist in ensemble {} anymore.&quot;&lt;/span&gt;, oldBookie, ensemble);
+        }
&lt;/pre&gt;
